<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Velbazhd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1330</span> · Also known as Battle of Velbužd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyustendil">Velbazhd</a> was fought on 28 July 1330 near Velbazhd, modern Kyustendil in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, between the Serbian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-decanski">Stefan Dečanski</a> and the Bulgarian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-shishman">Michael Shishman</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, with the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> leading the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry">heavy cavalry</a>, won a decisive victory and Michael Shishman was killed. The battle left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> the dominant power in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-velbazhd.jpg" alt="Battle of Velbazhd" width="320" height="126" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: late 16th-century fresco painter of Visoki Dečani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Velbu%C5%BEd,_detail_from_Visoki_De%C4%8Dani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
